cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization or its ring extension, please cite this repository and the upstream mathematical sources identified in README.md and NOTICE."
type: software
title: "Shared-leg rectangular matrix multiplication over arbitrary rings"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhou
    given-names: Yang
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Mingsheng
date-released: "2026-10-14"
url: "https://github.com/Hugin-Hilbert/rectangular-matmul-rings"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hugin-Hilbert/rectangular-matmul-rings"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization of rectangular matrix multiplication over every
  associative ring, including noncommutative and nonunital rings. The
  ring-independent arithmetic circuits give square matrix multiplication
  exponent at most 9/4 (2.25), dual exponent at least 1/2, and the shared-leg
  rectangular exponent curve, with arbitrary positive exponent slack.
  Includes the research note, integral tensor constructions, finite identity
  checks, and a proof correspondence. The rectangular bound originates in
  Przemyslaw Uznanski's arXiv:2610.10494; source provenance is in NOTICE.
keywords:
  - matrix multiplication
  - rectangular matrix multiplication
  - matrix multiplication exponent
  - dual exponent
  - arbitrary rings
  - noncommutative rings
  - nonunital rings
  - integral tensor rank
  - shared-leg entropy
  - arithmetic circuits
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
